WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:05.550
Let’s collect the traps, because the people who write the exam know every one of them.

2
00:00:05.800 --> 00:00:07.325
Bearings.

3
00:00:07.575 --> 00:00:11.575
Use the deviation for the boat’s heading, not for the bearing.

4
00:00:11.825 --> 00:00:13.325
Signs.

5
00:00:13.575 --> 00:00:15.800
Toward compass, add west.

6
00:00:16.050 --> 00:00:18.100
Toward true, add east.

7
00:00:18.350 --> 00:00:19.925
The rose.

8
00:00:20.175 --> 00:00:25.275
Read the wrong side, and your answer is exactly one hundred eighty degrees off.

9
00:00:25.525 --> 00:00:28.600
And will that wrong answer be among the choices?

10
00:00:29.600 --> 00:00:31.550
Very often, yes.

11
00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:35.575
Don’t mix true and magnetic in the same calculation.

12
00:00:35.825 --> 00:00:37.775
Pick one and stay in it.

13
00:00:38.025 --> 00:00:40.825
And answer in what the question asks for.

14
00:00:41.075 --> 00:00:45.350
If it says compass, a perfect true course is still a wrong answer.

15
00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:47.500
That’s lesson five.

16
00:00:47.750 --> 00:00:49.650
Write the chain on paper.

17
00:00:49.900 --> 00:00:52.425
Deviation goes with the heading.

18
00:00:52.675 --> 00:00:55.575
And read the last line of the question twice.

19
00:00:55.825 --> 00:00:59.175
Next time: lines of position and fixes.
